        "original_id": "d2daa569-c01b-501e-96da-d2e18dc18013",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Henderson Executive Airport, McCarran International Airport, Las Vegas\n- Organizations: Clark County, Democratic Party\n- People: Pat McCarran\n- Concepts: reliever airport, aviation development\n\nFacts:\n- Henderson Executive Airport was originally known as Sky Harbor Airport.\n- In 1996, Clark County purchased Sky Harbor Airport and renamed it Henderson Executive Airport.\n- In 1996, Clark County designated Henderson Executive Airport to serve as a reliever airport for McCarran International Airport.\n- McCarran International Airport is named after Pat McCarran.\n- Pat McCarran was a U.S. Senator and a member of the Democratic Party.\n- Pat McCarran contributed to the development of aviation in Las Vegas and across the United States.",
